  "memorial_details": "A copper and bronze plaque mounted on a wood backboard affixed to a tree.\n\nThe inscription mentions 'THE ENTIRE CREW OF THE LANCASTER PERISHED' and the community connection is implied by the memorial being erected for those who died.",
  "inscription": "WELLINGTONIA GIGANTEA/ THIS TREE WAS STRUCK BY LANCASTER MK III ME442 KM-V / OF BOMBER COMMAND R.A.F. SHOT DOWN IN FLAMES / BY A JU 188 ON THE NIGHT OF 3/4 MARCH 1945 / THE ENTIRE CREW OF THE LANCASTER PERISHED./ THE CREW COMPRISED/ FG OFF J J F RYAN RAAF/ SGT T H JARMAN/ FLT SGT R R RUSSELL/ FLT SGT H J TERRY/ SGT H BIRTCH/ SGT H PAYNE/ SGT W H ROGAN/ MAY THEY REST IN PEACE",
